> Traveling through Virginia to visit a close friend and family, I parked my car in Richmond. I heard of a great southern tradition that sounded[ delicious.] I had to give[ it a] try before venturing off on the road again to my next destination. Sally Bell[s Kitchen,] opened 90 years ago in 1924[.] The[ establishment was] founded by Sarah Cab[ell] Jones[ and] a business partner[.] Sarah and partner met at the Women’[s Exchange,] a former nationwide movement, intended to teach women skills and financial independence[.]
Sally Bell[s] Kitchen is known for their delicious boxed[ lunches. Items] such as potato[ salad], chicken[ salad], tuna[ salad], deviled eggs, cheese[ w]af[ers] and an array of cup[ cakes] are made fresh from scratch daily. They sell thousands of sandwiches, cup[cakes] and hundreds of pounds of salads each year. This establishment[ is] very welcoming, friendly and certainly has southern charm. The staff[ is] just[ wonderful!]

